// stdlib/noise_proto: BLAKE2s against RFC 7693 ("abc") and Python hashlib (empty, keyed, 16-byte keyed); then the Noise handshakes NN, NK, XX, IK (ChaChaPoly, SHA256), XX with AESGCM and SHA512, IKpsk2 with BLAKE2s and NNpsk0, with fixed static and ephemeral keys and prologue "John Galt": every message, the handshake hash, the first transport message each way and one after Rekey, byte-exact against an independent Node.js (OpenSSL) implementation; then a tampered message, a wrong pre-known key, a bad name and an out-of-turn write are refused.
// Expected output:
// blake2s abc 508c5e8c327c14e2e1a72ba34eeb452f37458b209ed63a294d999b4c86675982
// blake2s empty 69217a3079908094e11121d042354a7c1f55b6482ca1a51e1b250dfd1ed0eef9
